NativeAOT: leave the GC info out of the LSDA for a GC that never scans a stack (IlcZkNoGcInfo)

Every managed method's LSDA in .dotnet_eh_table carries the method's GC info after the flags and the
associated data and EH info pointers. Only a stack scan of the GC reads it (EnumGcRefs, IsSafePoint,
return address hijacking), and the unwind of a reverse P/Invoke frame. A zkVM guest links a GC that
never collects (uGC zero), so the tables an exception needs are mostly GC info no one reads: on the
Nethermind Airbender guest .dotnet_eh_table is 182,220 bytes, 161,000 of them GC info, and the unwind
tables do not fit in the 4 MiB ROM next to the code.

The backend option IlcZkNoGcInfo=1 (default: unchanged) sets ObjectWritingOptions.OmitGcInfo: the
main LSDA of a method that is not a reverse P/Invoke ends after its pointers. The LSDA cache compares
LSDAs by what is emitted, so the many methods that now differ only by their GC info share one blob.
The compiler reads the option itself; the JIT does not know the name. A guest turns it on with the
JIT options that rely on the same fact (JitZkNoGcMustInit).

Only valid when no stack is ever scanned: a GC that reads a frame would decode the bytes that follow.

Checked on the Nethermind Airbender guest with the same change made after the link (bflat patch_elf):
.dotnet_eh_table 182,220 -> 4,877 bytes together with dropping frameless leaf FDEs; blocks 11957686,
11962410, 25526356 give the same digests; exception tests (caught exception with finally, checked
conversions, gvm suite) pass.

